{"name":"Nocturnal Sea","hex":"#0e6071","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nocturnal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a person, creature, group, or species, primarily active during the night.","Of an occurrence, taking place at night, nightly."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person or creature that is active at night.","A device for telling the time at night, rather like a sundial but read according to the stars."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nocturnal"},{"term":"sea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Semai."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large body of salt water.","The ocean; the continuous body of salt water covering a majority of the Earth's surface."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nocturnal animal","blocks":[{"text":"Nocturnality is a behavior in some non-human animals characterized by being active during the night and sleeping during the day. The common adjective is nocturnal, with diurnal meaning the opposite."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Owl_at_Night.jpg/330px-Owl_at_Night.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nocturnal_animal","wikidata":"Q309179"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea","wikidata":"Q165"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://t